WEBVTT

00:01.510 --> 00:03.370
Three years ago,

00:03.710 --> 00:05.640
a pain reliever called Hapna,

00:05.660 --> 00:08.240
which claimed to liberate people from pain,

00:08.270 --> 00:10.430
began circulating on the streets.

00:10.450 --> 00:12.280
For young people,

00:12.540 --> 00:14.550
it held a special meaning.

00:15.890 --> 00:19.120
Hapna was used as a substitute drug.

00:19.140 --> 00:22.260
Mixing it into soda gave a euphoric high,

00:22.280 --> 00:23.900
perfect for when you were feeling down.

00:24.230 --> 00:28.440
All the young people chose it as a way to vent.

00:29.520 --> 00:31.180
Meanwhile, adults were all wondering,

00:31.200 --> 00:34.660
"Why are kids

00:34.690 --> 00:36.480
only drinking soda?"

00:37.150 --> 00:38.980
Anyway, to obtain Hapna,

00:39.180 --> 00:42.310
all one needed was a doctor's prescription.

00:42.620 --> 00:44.350
In short, it was "cheap."

00:45.220 --> 00:50.260
No one knew this would lead to an irreparable ending.

00:50.940 --> 00:52.040
Of course,

00:52.340 --> 00:54.770
I was one of them.

02:23.600 --> 02:29.520
[LAZARUS]

02:31.220 --> 02:33.450
You can't take that wristband off.

02:33.480 --> 02:36.690
It tracks your location constantly.

02:36.710 --> 02:37.630
So running is pointless.

02:40.320 --> 02:42.310
I see.

02:43.079 --> 02:46.120
Looks like everyone here has their own circumstances.

02:46.320 --> 02:47.960
What I want to ask of you all

02:48.050 --> 02:49.070
is to be the first

02:49.090 --> 02:52.350
to find Dr. Skinner.

02:52.980 --> 02:54.070
Think about it.

02:54.410 --> 02:57.140
Would you rather keep running as fugitives

02:57.160 --> 02:59.650
or find Skinner and win your freedom?

03:00.050 --> 03:01.410
Which would you choose?

03:10.500 --> 03:11.770
Hey.

03:11.800 --> 03:14.300
I choose an eye for an eye.

03:14.320 --> 03:16.470
Could you take off the wristband for me?

03:19.310 --> 03:21.370
Well, Hersch...

03:21.950 --> 03:23.700
I won't fall for the same trick twice.

03:24.510 --> 03:25.880
Ouch.

03:26.600 --> 03:29.230
If you forcibly remove it, the voltage will spike,

03:29.250 --> 03:30.410
and your arm will melt off.

03:31.040 --> 03:32.560
Just so you know,

03:32.590 --> 03:35.980
if anything happens to me, you'll end up the same way.

03:37.780 --> 03:39.040
Fine.

03:39.070 --> 03:42.160
I also wanted to meet that Skinner fellow, anyway.

03:42.350 --> 03:45.310
Finally, we're all on the same page.

03:45.960 --> 03:51.120
[Episode 2: Life in the Fast Lane]

03:51.140 --> 03:53.079
Why did the FDA

03:53.110 --> 03:54.630
approve this drug?

03:54.660 --> 03:59.660
There's no precedent for a drug that mutates after 3 years.

03:59.690 --> 04:01.710
Does this mean you didn't anticipate that?

04:01.730 --> 04:03.850
How will the government take responsibility?

04:03.880 --> 04:06.160
When do you plan to resign?

04:06.180 --> 04:06.980
Next,

04:07.010 --> 04:09.420
regarding the truth about Dr. Skinner's whereabouts,

04:09.450 --> 04:12.050
let's ask the person who has been managing his garden.

04:12.660 --> 04:15.590
Like that, did his gaze ever suddenly

04:15.610 --> 04:17.350
become very sharp?

04:17.600 --> 04:18.880
Oh my, I told you,

04:18.910 --> 04:21.329
I'm only responsible for maintaining the garden.

04:21.350 --> 04:22.220
Or

04:22.240 --> 04:24.800
did he ever say he couldn't understand how ordinary people think?

04:25.330 --> 04:27.280
Speaking of which...

04:27.310 --> 04:28.480
Speaking of which?

04:28.500 --> 04:30.870
I once buried a cat in the yard.

04:30.900 --> 04:33.230
A... a dead cat?

04:33.250 --> 04:35.030
His name was Moppet,

04:35.409 --> 04:37.740
a very cute cat.

04:37.900 --> 04:40.720
It died naturally.

04:42.590 --> 04:45.500
Lisa, you're finally about to release your new album next month,

04:45.520 --> 04:49.620
"See You Later," yet at this time,

04:49.650 --> 04:52.290
something big happened.

04:52.909 --> 04:54.720
Perhaps no one

04:54.740 --> 04:57.120
will have the chance to hear that album now.

04:58.900 --> 05:01.040
Yes.

05:01.060 --> 05:04.470
In that case, perhaps no one will watch this show either, right?

05:07.100 --> 05:08.500
Be right back,

05:08.520 --> 05:09.600
Crocodile.

05:12.250 --> 05:19.250
[Barber Shop]

05:13.830 --> 05:16.140
So, what do we do after we find Skinner?

05:16.700 --> 05:19.320
So, we could use him however we want?

05:19.370 --> 05:20.270
Use him?

05:20.660 --> 05:21.720
For example,

05:21.740 --> 05:23.810
monopolizing the antidote

05:23.840 --> 05:25.910
and selling it at jacked-up prices, that sort of thing.

05:26.170 --> 05:28.300
So, this is what it's all about.

05:28.320 --> 05:29.680
That's not what this is about.

05:29.750 --> 05:32.620
We're not gathered here

05:32.640 --> 05:34.140
for those selfish reasons.

05:34.159 --> 05:35.930
Then for what?

05:35.950 --> 05:36.960
For...

05:38.590 --> 05:40.380
saving the world, that kind of thing.

05:40.409 --> 05:43.020
So, we're the messengers of justice this time?

05:43.040 --> 05:45.920
So, like the Avengers?

05:45.950 --> 05:47.790
In short,

05:48.170 --> 05:51.880
right now, all we need to do is find a way to catch Skinner.

05:52.040 --> 05:54.650
Hey, can I ask you one thing?

05:55.420 --> 05:58.520
Has anyone here ever used Hapna?

06:09.230 --> 06:12.320
From now on, this is our base.

06:12.530 --> 06:16.210
Not gonna lie, but I was against you joining.

06:16.230 --> 06:17.350
Why?

06:17.380 --> 06:20.420
You have no coordination, just some flashy guy who wants attention.

06:20.450 --> 06:22.190
In a team like ours,

06:22.210 --> 06:23.510
that's a liability.

06:24.200 --> 06:25.600
But then again,

06:25.630 --> 06:29.640
isn't this place too shabby for the heroes' base?

06:29.670 --> 06:32.050
This is just a disguise.

06:32.070 --> 06:33.710
Really?

06:35.610 --> 06:36.659
Ah.

06:42.690 --> 06:43.780
Place your hand over it.

06:43.800 --> 06:45.310
It scans capillaries

06:45.330 --> 06:47.280
to grant you access.

06:54.790 --> 06:57.000
Have I been registered already?

06:57.020 --> 06:59.000
I did it while you were asleep.

07:00.430 --> 07:03.340
[Deniz Skinner]

07:01.260 --> 07:02.680
Deniz Skinner,

07:03.000 --> 07:04.680
if he's still alive, he'd be 56 this year.

07:03.340 --> 07:07.340
[Early life and education]

07:05.170 --> 07:06.390
Born in Istanbul.

07:07.090 --> 07:10.550
At 12, he lost both of his parents to a war.

07:07.340 --> 07:09.620
[Career and research]

07:10.790 --> 07:11.860
Afterwards,

07:11.890 --> 07:14.570
he never got married or had any children.

07:14.590 --> 07:17.010
What you'd call dying alone.

07:17.270 --> 07:20.370
[Tel Aviv—the early days.]

07:17.930 --> 07:20.860
Entered ETH Zurich at 16.

07:20.370 --> 07:23.940
[Enrolled at ETH Zurich, 2012, aged 16.]

07:21.080 --> 07:24.050
Graduated from Cambridge graduate school at 20.

07:23.940 --> 07:27.440
[At a café in University of Cambridge, circa 2016-2018]

07:24.070 --> 07:27.730
And since his student days, he's continuously achieved remarkable results.

07:27.440 --> 07:30.980
[Same café, same time period.]

07:28.270 --> 07:29.640
Since that time,

07:29.670 --> 07:31.230
he has been called

07:30.980 --> 07:32.350
[Playing hockey, likely during the Cambridge year]

07:31.260 --> 07:32.730
"The genius second only to Einstein."

07:32.760 --> 07:35.740
Objection. Rather than those things,

07:35.760 --> 07:39.640
isn't it better to introduce something about him related to his motives?

07:39.659 --> 07:40.740
Indeed.

07:42.730 --> 07:46.020
Skinner won the Nobel Prize three times.

07:46.180 --> 07:48.010
He donated most of the prize money to others

07:48.120 --> 07:50.480
while living a modest life himself.

07:51.070 --> 07:54.740
He gave up all patents related to the drugs he developed.

07:54.770 --> 07:56.159
Is that so?

07:56.280 --> 07:58.620
He was very active in peace movements and social activities

07:58.650 --> 08:01.660
aimed at eliminating wealth disparity.

08:01.930 --> 08:04.990
He was particularly concerned about climate issues.

08:03.310 --> 08:07.170
[COP49]

08:05.400 --> 08:08.240
He also attended environmental summits and UN meetings,

08:08.490 --> 08:10.730
continuously addressing this issue.

08:11.440 --> 08:12.660
This is

08:12.680 --> 08:15.060
his famous speech at the UN.

08:15.330 --> 08:17.100
I am merely

08:17.310 --> 08:20.270
stating facts as a scientist.

08:20.740 --> 08:22.440
According to my calculations,

08:22.630 --> 08:24.600
within three years,

08:25.060 --> 08:27.840
all the Arctic ice caps will melt completely.

08:28.240 --> 08:32.179
[Sierra Leone]

08:28.300 --> 08:29.140
But that's only

08:29.160 --> 08:30.920
the beginning.

08:31.330 --> 08:33.570
If we don't take action now,

08:33.590 --> 08:36.260
the Earth will collapse like an avalanche.

08:36.320 --> 08:39.620
[United States]

08:36.789 --> 08:38.909
If there are no humans living on Earth,

08:38.940 --> 08:41.909
what's the point of economic activities?

08:45.260 --> 08:46.550
In the end,

08:46.770 --> 08:49.650
the speech led to a terrible outcome: countries

08:49.750 --> 08:52.260
withdrew from the UN Security Council as permanent members.

08:53.650 --> 08:55.000
Shortly after this,

08:55.270 --> 08:57.010
he disappeared.

08:57.650 --> 08:59.680
He seems like a good boy.

08:59.700 --> 09:01.120
Too good. Feels fake.

09:01.470 --> 09:03.580
Who knows what he does behind the scenes?

09:03.840 --> 09:05.800
What about the online leaks of people who claimed to have seen him?

09:05.830 --> 09:09.260
There was such a post not long ago.

09:09.190 --> 09:12.770
[Then my friend told me he's like a genius scientist???]

09:09.190 --> 09:12.770
[I just saw this guy giving his seat to an old grandma on the train.]

09:09.670 --> 09:13.130
About him giving his seat to an elderly woman on the train.

09:12.880 --> 09:15.810
[I was feeling a bit down, but this honestly restored my faith in humanity.]

09:13.160 --> 09:15.740
Helping a homeless person in trouble.

09:16.090 --> 09:18.510
There was even a news bit about his sandwich

09:18.540 --> 09:20.690
getting stolen by a dog.

09:20.720 --> 09:21.790
What is all this?

09:21.810 --> 09:23.610
He's increasingly portrayed as a good boy.

09:23.630 --> 09:25.750
He's practically a saint.

09:25.770 --> 09:29.340
Why would someone like that do such a thing?

09:29.370 --> 09:30.780
In short, there's no information about him

09:30.800 --> 09:34.740
after he disappeared three years ago.

09:35.090 --> 09:38.400
Skinner left no trace anywhere.

09:38.830 --> 09:43.130
Has he been living self-sufficiently at home all this time?

09:43.150 --> 09:44.590
Could he actually be dead already?

09:44.610 --> 09:46.710
Or going out in disguise?

09:46.730 --> 09:49.320
There's a possibility that he's impersonating someone else.

09:49.880 --> 09:50.680
Well...

09:50.710 --> 09:51.440
-Yes?
-Yes?

09:52.040 --> 09:53.620
I found...

09:53.640 --> 09:55.110
a trace of him.

10:18.690 --> 10:19.990
That's why I told you

10:20.020 --> 10:22.210
not to drive so recklessly!

10:22.240 --> 10:23.560
You're right.

10:24.410 --> 10:26.460
Wow.

10:32.770 --> 10:34.650
Nuclear Shelter Trading Company?

10:35.240 --> 10:36.110
Yes.

10:36.260 --> 10:40.450
There's a record of Dr. Skinner buying from them 8 years ago.

10:40.890 --> 10:42.220
I see.

10:42.500 --> 10:44.510
If it's a nuclear shelter,

10:44.530 --> 10:47.550
he can live for years without seeing a single person.

10:47.570 --> 10:49.560
It's just that the company

10:49.580 --> 10:51.750
won't respond to any emails or phone calls.

10:52.140 --> 10:54.030
Axel and Chris, go check the shelter.

10:54.050 --> 10:55.430
Doug and Leland,

10:55.460 --> 10:57.060
go check the trading company.

10:57.320 --> 10:58.260
Eleina,

10:58.510 --> 11:02.020
can you run facial recognition for Dr. Skinner

11:02.040 --> 11:04.570
across all surveillance records worldwide?

11:04.600 --> 11:05.790
I can.

11:08.480 --> 11:12.190
If he's disguised as someone else, it won't work,

11:13.240 --> 11:15.600
but it's worth a shot.

11:22.870 --> 11:24.210
You...

11:24.230 --> 11:25.970
were in prison, right?

11:26.000 --> 11:28.270
Ah... sort of.

11:28.480 --> 11:29.920
What crime did you commit?

11:30.140 --> 11:31.680
How long was your sentence?

11:31.890 --> 11:33.660
It was...

11:33.680 --> 11:35.460
888 years.

11:38.990 --> 11:39.450
Get out of the car,

11:39.690 --> 11:41.560
you murderous devil!

11:41.720 --> 11:45.590
How dare you sit here on what seems like a joyride with that carefree expression!

11:45.610 --> 11:46.490
Wait a minute!

11:46.510 --> 11:47.910
If you hadn't killed just one person,

11:47.930 --> 11:49.650
there's no way you'd get such a long sentence.

11:49.670 --> 11:50.890
Let me explain.

11:50.920 --> 11:52.420
How many people did you kill?

11:53.190 --> 11:54.100
Do you know

11:54.120 --> 11:57.760
that your sentence can be doubled each time you escape from prison?

11:58.850 --> 11:59.530
So?

11:59.560 --> 12:01.300
It was three years at first.

12:01.530 --> 12:03.850
But I kept escaping, and before I knew it,

12:03.880 --> 12:06.060
it became that many.

12:06.600 --> 12:07.640
What?

12:07.660 --> 12:10.160
Why did you escape so frequently?

12:10.780 --> 12:12.200
Because...

12:13.600 --> 12:14.550
it's a hobby, I guess.

12:15.690 --> 12:16.810
Seriously.

12:17.160 --> 12:19.130
What kind of reason is that?

12:22.950 --> 12:25.920
Doug, if you know that wristband,

12:25.950 --> 12:28.690
does that mean you also know about its weakness?

12:28.710 --> 12:30.170
Do you want to know?

12:30.610 --> 12:32.640
Yes, a little.

12:32.660 --> 12:35.160
Curiosity kills the cat.

12:35.180 --> 12:37.730
Is it going to be that serious?

12:37.750 --> 12:39.750
It's just a metaphor.

12:39.780 --> 12:43.320
For me, it's just going to be a minor injury.

12:43.340 --> 12:45.550
A minor injury?

12:46.370 --> 12:48.700
What about you, Leland?

12:48.780 --> 12:51.300
For me, it's really not a big deal.

12:51.560 --> 12:53.230
Just some theft and stuff.

12:53.260 --> 12:55.170
It's really not a big deal.

12:56.960 --> 12:59.920
Compared to us, the punishment for Eleina would be even more severe.

12:59.940 --> 13:01.450
Really?

13:01.750 --> 13:05.640
Seems like she's a notorious hacker who caused many incidents.

13:07.080 --> 13:09.550
She seems so well-behaved.

13:09.580 --> 13:11.030
In fact,

13:11.340 --> 13:13.980
she might be the real boss here.

13:22.520 --> 13:31.470
[LAZARUS]

13:36.090 --> 13:41.310
[Shelter Area B, Arizona]

14:00.190 --> 14:05.260
[Kobayashi Shelter Sales]

14:11.520 --> 14:13.320
Is this really the place?

14:13.350 --> 14:15.430
It should be.

14:22.220 --> 14:24.790
B12... Is this it?

14:25.040 --> 14:27.260
There's no one.

14:29.530 --> 14:30.450
Let's go.

14:52.330 --> 14:54.280
Self-powered?

14:54.300 --> 14:57.110
All we can see is rubble.

15:15.000 --> 15:18.210
Hello.

15:18.230 --> 15:20.040
Amigo.

15:20.060 --> 15:22.160
Hello. Is anyone here?

15:26.360 --> 15:28.790
There are traces of someone working here recently.

16:08.010 --> 16:09.430
Is this man

16:09.460 --> 16:10.430
Skinner?

16:10.910 --> 16:11.980
No.

16:12.010 --> 16:14.040
Maybe he had plastic surgery.

16:14.220 --> 16:16.220
Hey, still alive?

16:19.570 --> 16:21.950
Oh, drop the gun.

16:21.950 --> 16:23.270
Drop it slowly.

16:23.580 --> 16:25.130
I'm sorry.

16:28.910 --> 16:29.860
Sorry,

16:29.890 --> 16:31.410
I'm also here for business.

16:31.710 --> 16:33.090
Where is he?

16:33.110 --> 16:33.930
Who?

16:34.290 --> 16:36.400
Tell me now.

16:36.430 --> 16:38.430
That way, I won't have to complete my task brutally.

16:38.540 --> 16:39.570
Wait, hold on.

16:39.590 --> 16:41.180
We don't know either.

16:41.750 --> 16:43.750
If you're still going to play dumb,

16:43.770 --> 16:45.770
I have my own way.

16:46.520 --> 16:47.830
Make your choice.

16:47.850 --> 16:50.040
Your nose or your ear?

16:50.060 --> 16:53.720
Kill all those who get in the way!

16:56.080 --> 16:57.600
Kill them as a sacrifice!

16:57.630 --> 16:58.800
What?

17:03.090 --> 17:06.400
Ding-dong, the guest is here.

17:06.430 --> 17:09.260
Okay, Kobayashi, come out! Kobayashi!

17:11.140 --> 17:12.140
Kobayashi?

17:12.760 --> 17:14.780
Darn it, they popped out of nowhere!

17:15.180 --> 17:16.540
They are...

17:16.569 --> 17:18.210
Russians.

17:18.240 --> 17:19.700
You understand Russian?

17:19.730 --> 17:22.780
Kill everyone except the doctor!

17:22.810 --> 17:24.510
The ones here are more likely from Chicago.

17:30.250 --> 17:32.460
Looks like you're quite enjoying this.

17:32.480 --> 17:33.880
You caught me.

17:35.850 --> 17:36.680
What is this?

17:37.490 --> 17:38.710
It's a spell.

17:38.740 --> 17:41.510
This angel has always been watching over me.

17:41.510 --> 17:42.730
What?

17:42.760 --> 17:44.500
As long as she's with me,

17:45.220 --> 17:47.220
I won't die.

17:50.630 --> 17:51.310
That guy...

17:51.330 --> 17:53.490
is really crazy.

17:58.140 --> 18:00.690
Kobayashi, you're here, right?

18:00.710 --> 18:03.850
Today, you must pay me back everything!

18:04.180 --> 18:05.730
What are you talking about?

18:05.970 --> 18:08.390
Are you not Skinner?

18:08.420 --> 18:09.820
Who are you?

18:09.850 --> 18:11.310
I'm a debt collector!

18:11.310 --> 18:13.390
So am I!

18:29.620 --> 18:30.280
Try this, you jerk!

18:30.300 --> 18:31.550
And this!

18:31.580 --> 18:32.970
What's happening here?

18:56.450 --> 18:57.300
Hey!

18:57.420 --> 18:59.370
Shouldn't Skinner be our top priority now?

18:59.370 --> 19:01.640
Seems like it.

19:12.490 --> 19:13.910
Don't move!

19:14.470 --> 19:16.470
FBI! Drop your weapon!

19:16.690 --> 19:18.970
DEA! Drop your weapons!

19:19.050 --> 19:21.050
Lazarus! Drop your weapon!

19:21.210 --> 19:21.960
What?

19:22.730 --> 19:23.890
Lazarus?

19:23.920 --> 19:25.500
What's that?

19:27.800 --> 19:29.540
We are messengers of justice.

19:44.710 --> 19:45.560
No...

19:48.410 --> 19:51.510
I'm so sorry!

19:51.660 --> 19:55.040
I didn't mean to run away.

19:55.060 --> 19:56.220
I was going to pay you back slowly.

19:56.240 --> 19:57.740
Don't kill me!

19:57.770 --> 19:59.380
Please forgive me!

19:59.760 --> 20:02.040
You're...

20:02.070 --> 20:05.010
not Skinner?

20:05.920 --> 20:07.310
Ouch!

20:12.150 --> 20:14.150
DNA identification complete.

20:14.730 --> 20:16.730
He's someone else.

20:20.280 --> 20:23.940
Kobayashi, that jerk, you still lent money to a shut-in like that?

20:24.160 --> 20:28.260
All of last month's concrete fees.

20:28.430 --> 20:30.670
That's really not easy.

20:30.690 --> 20:33.760
Right? He's got to be kidding me.

20:33.780 --> 20:35.780
Sorry, kid.

20:36.040 --> 20:38.040
I thought you were with him.

20:38.230 --> 20:39.440
It's okay.

20:39.580 --> 20:42.380
You guys are also looking for Kobayashi, right?

20:42.840 --> 20:44.470
We're after a completely different guy.

20:44.490 --> 20:45.220
Ah,

20:45.320 --> 20:48.610
hiding in the shelter he built himself.

20:49.190 --> 20:50.620
Not only that,

20:50.640 --> 20:53.810
but the FBI and others have all come in large numbers.

20:54.760 --> 20:55.670
Got it.

20:59.320 --> 21:00.510
Looks like

21:00.730 --> 21:03.010
it's not a simple mission at all.

21:03.040 --> 21:05.200
-Good, good!
-Stop it!

21:05.200 --> 21:07.030
-Haha!
-Haha!

21:10.990 --> 21:13.720
Come to think of it, I've lived my whole life relying on luck.

21:14.370 --> 21:16.120
Always wanted to hit the jackpot once

21:16.290 --> 21:19.960
and become rich.

21:20.530 --> 21:23.950
I never thought

21:24.000 --> 21:26.360
this would be the end of my life.

21:27.080 --> 21:31.590
I thought I'd die after eating Hapna.

21:32.140 --> 21:35.240
But it turns out Hapna doesn't kill you right away.

21:36.780 --> 21:39.920
No. Is this...

21:40.750 --> 21:43.290
a sign telling me to give life another shot?

21:44.410 --> 21:45.260
How about...

21:45.930 --> 21:48.240
I start over?

21:51.830 --> 21:54.330
No.

21:54.700 --> 21:56.700
In 30 days,

21:56.730 --> 21:58.730
we're all going to die.

22:00.640 --> 22:02.420
Found him,

22:02.440 --> 22:03.820
Dr. Skinner.

22:04.230 --> 22:04.880
Where is he?

22:07.330 --> 22:11.080
Dr. Skinner...

22:11.100 --> 22:12.910
There are about 100,000 of him.

22:12.930 --> 22:15.490
What's going on here?

22:15.570 --> 22:18.650
[28 Days Left...]
